FirstMetSupCal: {
	Rolename1: ???
	Rolename2: Brimstone Witch
	Line1: I hadn't expected you to kill my 'sister' so soon.
	Line2: You are growing... faster than anticipated.
	Line3: I recognize you... You're...
	Line4: The Brimstone Witch?! The one who incinerated half the ocean?!
	Line5: Hah?! Heh... To think someone... or some*fish*... actually recognizes me. You are amusing, I'll give you that.
	Line6: ...But why are you alive? I distinctly remember the Brimstone Witch died... last century.
	Line7: An interesting fish, indeed. My consciousness was forged into the brimstone flame long ago. This body... it is merely a corpse, puppeteered by the flames.
	Line8: ...A living mind in an inhuman vessel, bound to the world by a medium... You've become... an aberration?!
	Line9: Your comprehension is too limited. You could not possibly understand my state of being.
	Line10: Besides, that is not why I am here...
	QuestionLine: Well... what is your choice?
	Choice1Text: (Draw weapon)
	Choice2Text: (Remain silent)
	Choice1Response: Then let me measure your worth.
	Choice2Response: ...Pathetic. A 'small fry', indeed. Very well, take this as a greeting gift. We will meet again.
	NoFishLine1: You killed my 'sister' far sooner than I expected. And you came alone?
	NoFishLine2: You are growing stronger than I anticipated.
	NoFishLine3: You ask why I am still alive? It seems you have begun to touch upon truths you were not meant to know.
	NoFishLine4: My consciousness was forged into the brimstone flame long ago. This body... is merely a corpse puppeteered by the flames.
	NoFishLine5: But it is pointless. Your comprehension is too limited to grasp my state of being.
	NoFishLine6: Of course, I did not reveal myself merely to explain these trivialities.
}

SupCalMoonLordReward: {
	Line1: Hahaha...
	Line2: So that's how far he's fallen.
	Line3: Do you have any idea what the underground looks like right now?
	Line4: ...So, why are you here this time?
	Line5: A little toy for you. And a small commission.
	Line6: A small crossbow. I need you to take it and kill that... *thing*... pathetically sucking up geothermal energy down there. And remember, you *must* use this crossbow.
	Line7: If you succeed, our... 'partnership'... can continue.
}

SupCalDefeat: {
	Rolename2: Halibut & [Name]
	Line1: To think you've already reached this level... Heh. I was outmatched.
	Line2: But you are not the strongest. You may be good, but *he* is certainly no worse than you.
	Line3: Yharim has already walked to the end of that path. He has reached the pinnacle of what a Terrarian can be. No one is stronger.
	Line4: A pity you two cannot meet...
	Line5: Your level of comprehension is too low. You will never understand my state.
	Line6: ...My level of comprehension is too low?
	Line7: (I've lived this long, and this is the first time anyone's told me my 'level' is low.)
	Line8: I am the sole being 'birthed' by an era. Since I dared to cast off my Terrarian identity and declare myself a god, I am naturally omnipotent.
	Line9: You say Yharim can 'weigh' me? You'd need to bring me Xeroc.
	Line10: ......
}

SupCalPlayerDefeat: {
	Line1: You shatter at a touch. Are you made of paper?
	Line2: I thought I'd found a toy that would last a bit longer in the fire.
	Line3: I overestimated you. Your current caliber... you aren't even worthy of being my warm-up.
	Line4: Come back when you are strong enough to be worthy of my gaze.
	Line5: Although... you do have *some* courage.
	Line6: A mortal who dares to look me in the eye, let alone draw a blade... you are the first.
	Line7: (Vanishes in a whirlwind of flame)
	Line8: If I'd opened the ninth eye, consequences be damned... I should have had a chance. If it came to that...
	Line9: Sigh...
}

SupCalVictory: {
	Line1: What... How is this possible!
	Line2: You... You defeated me?!
	Line3: Impossible... This is absolutely impossible...
	Line4: I have already surpassed the limits of a Terrarian...
	Line5: ...It seems I truly underestimated you.
	Line6: But this is not the end. I will return.
	Line7: Next time... Next time, I will not be so careless!
	Line8: ...She fled.
}

PallbearerQuestUI: {
	QuestTitle: Commission: Hunt the Profaned Goddess
	QuestDesc: Defeat the Profaned Goddess using only the Pallbearer.
	AcceptText: Accept
	DeclineText: Decline
}

SupCalQuestReward: {
	Line1: Well done.
	Line2: This crossbow suits you.
	Line3: You've solved a problem for me.
	Line4: As a reward, these are yours.
	Line5: And this blade. I need you to take it and kill that... *worm*. Don't worry, the payment will be even more generous.
	Line6: I've imbued it with a portion of my Brimstone... 'presence.' It should make things easier for you.
	Line7: ......
}

DoGQuestUI: {
	QuestTitle: Commission: The Devourer of Gods
	QuestDesc: Defeat The Devourer of Gods using the Heartcarver.
	AcceptText: Accept
	DeclineText: Decline
}

SupCalDoGQuestReward: {
	Line1: Cleanly done.
	Line2: This blade... as satisfying as ever.
	Line3: Back when I was still mortal, this is what I used to gouge out my master's heart. It works well, doesn't it?
	Line4: Take it.
	Line5: Have you ever considered... what you would do if, next time, my commission was for you to kill ME?
	Line6: Such a pity. You and he are fated never to meet. You two would have had... so much to talk about.
	Line7: ......I really can't stand her.
}

SupCalYharonQuestReward: {
	Line1: Ah... it's finally over.
	Line2: To me... that dragon... was one of the very few beings worthy of respect.
	Line3: Knowing it would die, yet still choosing to stand its ground... Even if it's revived by the Auric Soul, the one that returns is merely a copy.
	Line4: A pity. It excelled at obedience, while you excel at... hm, *surviving*?
	Line5: Take this. Auric Ingot. Once called the 'Gold of Purgatory,' it is the limit of power a mortal can touch.
	Line6: And now... it's my turn.
	Line7: What kind of joke is this...?
}

YharonQuestUI: {
	QuestTitle: Commission: The Dragon of Incineration
	QuestDesc: Use the Oni Machete to slay Yharon, the Incineration Dragon.
	AcceptText: Accept
	DeclineText: Decline
}

